      "writtenOn": "2023-09-19T16:17:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I still believe the sensor [stack] is not the root cause of the issue: another task is taking all the time, so while we are processing the bottom half, we get interrupted long enough for another sensor event to be available, leading to a watchdog timer in the sensor task.\n\nWe don\u0027t see a watchdog though, right? We just see the sensor task stop running its main loop but the sensor task itself _doesn\u0027t_ watchdog. That implies that something in the sensor task is infinite looping but there\u0027s a sleep in the loop to prevent the watchdog. The best guess was that the sleep was the sleep in the BMI register access functions and that the loop was here, but agreed that we don\u0027t have any definite proof.\n\nI don\u0027t think another task is sucking up all the time, though. Then that other task would watchdog, right? ...and also we are seeing the EC respond / work in general. It\u0027s just the sensor task not running.",
      "parentUuid": "06d79a3d_af92c2e6",
      "revId": "b242342b784a7e2a365c28cd502093fb2f9d19ef",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
